{%- comment -%}
  horizon-blocks Phase 13 — the `Theme` JS global.

  Dawn-side equivalent of the `const Theme` block from stock Horizon v4.1.1
  (68760d9) snippets/scripts.liquid:285-309, verbatim in shape. Rendered by
  layout/theme.liquid immediately after the @theme/* importmap — a classic
  inline script, so it executes before any deferred module (stock also
  declares Theme after its module script tags; every consumer reads it at
  event time, not module-eval time).

  Consumers in the ported surface: hz-product-form.js (routes.cart_add_url,
  routes.cart_url, translations.added), gift-card-recipient-form.js
  (translations.recipient_form_*). The remaining keys ship stock-shaped for
  future slices (quick-order-list reads items_added_to_cart_*, header-actions
  reads cart_count).

  ADAPT decisions:
  - Translations hardcoded to stock Horizon English (locales/en.default.json
    values) — Dawn's locale files don't carry the Horizon keys, and the
    port-wide precedent is t:-to-English hardcoding (Phase 1b onward).
    items_added_to_cart_other keeps the literal `{{ count }}` placeholder
    (raw-escaped below) — stock JS does the interpolation client-side
    (quick-order-list.js:575).
  - routes stay Liquid-sourced (Shopify-global routes object, identical in
    Dawn): cart_add_url gets the stock `.js` append — hz-product-form.js
    POSTs FormData to it and expects a JSON response. Dawn's own
    `window.routes` global (theme.liquid) is untouched; the two coexist.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  const Theme = {
    translations: {
      placeholder_image: `Placeholder image`,
      added: `Added`,
      recipient_form_fields_visible: `Recipient form fields are now visible`,
      recipient_form_fields_hidden: `Recipient form fields are now hidden`,
      recipient_form_error: `There was an error with the form submission`,
      items_added_to_cart_one: `1 item added to cart`,
      items_added_to_cart_other: `{% raw %}{{ count }}{% endraw %} items added to cart`,
      cart_count: `Total items in cart`,
    },
    routes: {
      cart_add_url: '{{ routes.cart_add_url | append: '.js' }}',
      cart_change_url: '{{ routes.cart_change_url }}',
      cart_update_url: '{{ routes.cart_update_url }}',
      cart_url: '{{ routes.cart_url }}',
      predictive_search_url: '{{ routes.predictive_search_url }}',
      search_url: '{{ routes.search_url }}',
    },
    template: {
      name: '{{ template }}',
    },
  };
</script>
